---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description="How UK Survival Kits sources guidance, labels evidence and separates advertising from editorial criteria."
  canonicalPath="/editorial-policy/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
      <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
      <h2>Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        We help UK households plan for disruption using official guidance first, then practical
        criteria, then optional product examples linked through Amazon Associates.
      </p>
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>
        Prefer UK government Be Ready materials, Ready Scotland, Met Office, Environment Agency /
        SEPA, Red Cross and other statutory or recognised public sources. Global uncertainty appears
        only with a dated, citable frame—never as prophecy.
      </p>
      <h2>Evidence labels</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Official guidance</strong> — paraphrase of government or agency advice with a link.</li>
        <li><strong>Desk research</strong> — specifications and standards without a physical test.</li>
        <li><strong>Firsthand test</strong> — author-used item with method notes; not presented as desk research.</li>
        <li><strong>Reader tip</strong> — moderated, unverified reader input.</li>
        <li><strong>Ad</strong> — affiliate or other advertising, labelled before engagement.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What we won't publish</h2>
      <p>
        Weapons recommendations, invented urgency, panic-buying prompts, or conflation of Scottish
        and England/Wales flood systems.
      </p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="/contact/">the editors</a>. Significant factual corrections are updated on the
        page with a revised date where practical.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
